      "title": "Canadian publisher Boréal ends relationship with novelist Thélyson Orélien over alleged use of AI",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/22/canadian-publisher-boreal-ends-relationship-author-thelyson-orelien-over-ai",
      "description": "<p>Author withdrawn from France’s Prix Goncourt last month has repeatedly denied using artificial intelligence to write novel</p><p>The publisher of top-selling Haitian Canadian writer Thélyson Orélien, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/sep/25/thelyson-orelien-goncourt-prize-france\">who was removed from France’s most prestigious literary prize list</a> last month, has confirmed the author used artificial intelligence to help write his novel C’était ça ou mourir (It Was Either That or Die).</p><p>Orélien has denied allegations that he used AI on his breakthrough novel and, last week, Canadian publisher Les Éditions du Boréal said it was standing by the 38-year-old writer.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2026/oct/22/canadian-publisher-boreal-ends-relationship-author-thelyson-orelien-over-ai\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-22T01:13:01"
    },
